# A value an override in a dispatch builds moves into the dispatch's frame when it opens
known #102 fault Notice@Post()/Post() stands in

# The shortcut's board: `pin` puts a Notice into the file, and `posts` gives back what the file holds as records, of no
# type of the code's: the Notice goes in and no type comes out. `posts` returns what it read, so it uses it, and the
# file stands between the put and the get as on the clean side.

route shortcut.files.Board
step Board()/Board()
step Board()/Board.pin
step Board()/Board.posts

line entry > Board()/Board() call
line entry > Board()/Board.pin call
line entry > Board()/Board.posts call
line Board()/Board() > Board@Board()/Board() value
known #74 line Board > Board()/Board.pin value   # the caller's instance: every method runs on it
known #74 line Board > Board()/Board.posts value
known #127 line Notice·notice > Board()/Board.pin value          # #127
line Board()/Board.pin > Disk(this.path) own
line Disk(this.path) > Board()/Board.posts own

home Board@Board()/Board() Board()
known #74 home Board Board()
known #127 home Notice·notice Board()

side entry left
known #76 side Disk(this.path) between                         # Atlas: right, as if what posts returns were unused

# #127: the parameter of a method the entry calls has lost its name
known #127 extra line Notice > Board()/Board.pin value
known #127 extra home Notice Board()

# what the constructor builds goes back to its caller: Atlas runs the methods on it instead of the caller's instance
known #74 extra line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.pin value
known #74 extra line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.posts value
